@aditimagrawal If you are delivering so many orders successfully and your business is doing well, then refunding customers to their original payment method should be a basic standard of customer service. A customer’s money should rightfully go back to the customer, not be held as wallet credit.

Giving refunds only as wallet credit makes it seem like customers are being forced to shop only from your website, even after having a disappointing experience. That does not feel fair or customer-friendly.

Simply stating it in your policy does not automatically make it reasonable. Good customer service is about prioritising customer convenience and trust, not restricting their money to your platform.
